{"name":"Highway to Hell","hex":"#cd1102","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"highway","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A main public road, especially a multi-lane, high-speed thoroughfare.","Any public road."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel on a highway"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highway"},{"term":"hell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place of torment where some or all sinners are believed to go after death and evil spirits are believed to be.","Synonym of underworld, an underground land of the dead without eternal punishment or with only some regions of punishment."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place or situation of great suffering in life.","A place for gambling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Highway to Hell","blocks":[{"text":"Highway to Hell is the sixth studio album by Australian hard rock band AC/DC, released on 27 July 1979, by Albert Productions and Atlantic Records. It is the first of three albums produced by Robert John \"Mutt\" Lange, and is the last album featuring lead singer Bon Scott, who died on 19 February 1980."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Acdc_Highway_to_Hell.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highway_to_Hell","wikidata":"Q285929"},{"title":"Highway to Hell (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Highway to Hell\" is a song by Australian rock band AC/DC. It is the opening track of their album Highway to Hell (1979), initially released as a single on 27 July 1979, the same day the album was released."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Highway_to_Hell_by_ACDC_US_single_side-A.png/330px-Highway_to_Hell_by_ACDC_US_single_side-A.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highway_to_Hell_(song)","wikidata":"Q1508213"},{"title":"Highway","blocks":[{"text":"A highway in the broadest sense of the term is any public or private road or other public way on land, including not just major roads but also other public roads and rights of way. In the United States, the term is used to describe major roads. It is sometimes used casually as a synonym of freeway, or expressway, denoting a controlled-access highway."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Street%2C_Oguz_%28P1090484%29.jpg/330px-Street%2C_Oguz_%28P1090484%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highway","wikidata":"Q269949"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ac/Acdc_Highway_to_Hell.JPG/250px-Acdc_Highway_to_Hell.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Acdc_Highway_to_Hell.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ac/Acdc_Highway_to_Hell.JPG/250px-Acdc_Highway_to_Hell.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAcdc_Highway_to_Hell.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c7/ACDC_Highway_To_Hell_AUS.jpg/250px-ACDC_Highway_To_Hell_AUS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c7/ACDC_Highway_To_Hell_AUS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c7/ACDC_Highway_To_Hell_AUS.jpg/250px-ACDC_Highway_To_Hell_AUS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AACDC_Highway_To_Hell_AUS.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co